---
// Terms of Service — PLACEHOLDER.
//
// This page exists so the consent checkbox in the enrollment flow links to a
// real URL instead of a 404. The enrollment flow asks people to agree to these
// terms, so the page they're agreeing to must at minimum resolve and say
// honestly that it isn't finished yet.
//
// Real content is a separate follow-up — source material and the open
// questions for the attorney are in docs/legal-source.md.
//
// Per docs/AUNT-MABEL.md § Entity & naming: the contracting party is
// Trustlight LLC, the for-profit operator. Cajun Navy Ground Force appears only
// as HERITAGE — where the service came from — never as the operator or the
// party you contract with. An earlier version of this page named Cajun Relief
// Foundation as the operator; that was wrong and is corrected here.
//
// 2026-08-10: the in-person disaster wellness check was removed from the
// product, so this page no longer describes it. A legal page that promises a
// service we do not provide is the worst place for that claim to survive — it
// is the document someone agrees to. The page now says plainly that there are
// no in-person visits, rather than simply going quiet on the subject.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalDraft from '../components/LegalDraft.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service · Aunt Mabel" noindex={true}>
  <LegalDraft heading="Terms of Service" kicker="Legal">
    <p>
      These Terms will govern your use of the Aunt Mabel daily wellness-call
      service, which is operated by <strong>Trustlight LLC</strong>. Trustlight LLC is
      the company you contract with and the company that takes payment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Aunt Mabel grew out of years of disaster-response work with the
      <strong>Cajun Navy Ground Force</strong>, and uses their name with their
      permission. That is the service's history, not a description of what it
      does: the Cajun Navy Ground Force does not operate Aunt Mabel, is not the
      party you contract with, and does not take your payment.
    </p>
    <p class="emphasis">
      Aunt Mabel does not provide in-person visits, disaster response, or
      wellness checks at anyone's home. The service is the daily phone call and
      the alerts that follow from it.
    </p>
    <p>
      These Terms are being finalized with counsel now. When they're ready, this
      page will carry the full Terms in plain language, covering what the service
      does and doesn't promise, how billing and cancellation work, and how and
      when we contact the people you name.
    </p>
    <p>
      Until then, one thing is worth saying plainly, because it's the point
      people most need to understand before they sign up:
    </p>
    <p class="emphasis">
      Aunt Mabel is a friendly daily check-in. It is not an emergency service,
      a medical service, or a monitoring service, and it is not a substitute
      for calling 911 or for professional care.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you have a question in the meantime, please get in touch before
      enrolling rather than after.
    </p>
  </LegalDraft>
</BaseLayout>
